  "summary": "This one-page telegram, sent by M. R. Masani on July 31, 1964, asks Prof. Ranga to come to Madras for an urgent meeting of the organisation subcommittee. Masani reports that a report from Munshi on Bihar indicates that twelve members of the party in the Assembly may defect, making an immediate organisational response necessary.\n\nMasani says that he has consulted Rajaji and is convening the meeting for 9 a.m. on Saturday, August 8. He asks Ranga to travel by plane on the night of August 7 and wire confirmation of his presence. The second rendered page is the verso of the telegram form, containing standard postal instructions and the legal conditions governing acceptance and delivery; it adds no further political content.",
